nt from all vertices $A, B, C, D$ of the tetrahedron, $P$ is the center of the circumsphere of the tetrahedron. \n\n2. **Understand Position of $Q$:**\n   Point $Q$ is the intersection of the line $\\overrightarrow{AP}$ with face $BCD$.\n\n3. **Symmetry and Geometry:**\n   - In a regular tetrahedron, the line connecting the center $P$ to any vertex (say $A$) passes through the centroid of the opposite face (face $BCD$).\n   - The centroid of an equilateral triangle divides each median into a ratio of $2:1$, with the longer segment being towards the vertex.\n\n4. **Locating $Q$:**\n   - Since $P$ is the circumcenter, extending $\\overrightarrow{AP}$ until it intersects face $BCD$ will pass through the centroid of the triangle $BCD$.\n   - Let’s denote the centroid of triangle $BCD$ as $G$. The line segment from $A$ to $G$ will pass through $P$.\n\n5. **Calculate the Ratio:**\n   - The centroid $G$ of triangle $BCD$ divides the median from $A$ to $G$ in the ratio $2:1$.\n   - Since $P$ is the circumcenter, it is also the centroid of the tetrahedron, and it divides the segment $AG$ in the ratio $3:1$ (from the vertex to the centroid).\n\n6. **Expressing $PQ$ and $AQ$:**\n   - If we consider the entire segment from $A$ to $G$ as $3$ units, then $P$ divides this segment such that $AP = 2$ units and $PG = 1$ unit.\n   - The segment $AQ$ would be $3$ units (from $A$ to $G$).\n   - The segment $PQ$ would be $1$ unit (from $P$ to $G$).\n\n7. **Final Calculation:**\n   The ratio $PQ/AQ$ is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{PQ}{AQ} = \\frac{1}{3}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the ratio $PQ/AQ$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
